    "body": "## Summary\n- apply the existing symmetric user-block policy to saved-search alert delivery\n- suppress `SAVED_SEARCH_MATCH` delivery rows and notifications when either the alert owner or job author has blocked the other\n- keep publication outbox events progressing normally so blocked matches do not get stuck or retried forever\n- add a regression test proving blocked matches create neither a delivery record nor a notification\n- document the new enforcement boundary\n\n## Safety / privacy\n- reverse-block state remains private; no API response exposes which side created the block\n- no exact location, route, live-tracking, escrow, payment or moderation data is added\n- active job lifecycle remains unchanged\n\n## Validation\nRun Maven verify, frontend lint/build and the repository's existing runtime/smoke workflows. Do not merge unless required checks are green.",
